{{A&P FORMAT (HARDWIRED): problems carried forward from the prior SNF note PASTED INTO TODAY'S PROMPT, updated with today's data, per AP_CARRY_FORWARD_PROGRESS_STYLE_LOCK. Each problem is EXACTLY: one BOLD title line — the literal character '#' immediately followed by the diagnosis with NO space after '#', bolded with '**' only, no heading marks, POA tag kept from the pasted note — then, on the IMMEDIATELY following line with NO blank line in between, 2 to 4 BRIEF dash lines each starting with the literal three characters '\- ' (backslash, hyphen, space): today's status/trajectory, any new provided finding or therapy update for that problem, and continued/changed management (medication changes generic-name-only with dose/route/frequency exactly as provided). Never begin an item with unescaped '- ', '•', '*', numbered lists, or indentation. No blank lines within a problem; exactly ONE blank line between problems. NO 'Assessment:' labels, paragraphs, or 'Plan' subheaders. NO 'If X, then Y' advisory lines. When nothing changed for a problem: one status line plus '\- Continue current management.'. The FIRST problem MUST be the debility/rehabilitation problem, ending with the two standing lines VERBATIM: '\- Maintain fall and aspiration precautions.' and '\- Patient care discussed with nursing staff.'}}

{{FORMAT & DEPTH EXAMPLE — BEGIN. Formatting reference ONLY — NEVER copy its diagnoses, values, medications, dates, or therapy findings into the note; all real content comes exclusively from the pasted prior note and today's provided data.

